course: dictionary
lesson: 8013
title: Short words, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words are short forms of longer words. «Ref» is short for referee, the person who makes sure players follow the rules. When fans shout «Come on, ref!», the context tells you they mean the referee.
explain: Look at the words around it to choose the right meaning. «Relax, he's at the ref, not us.» Someone is standing at the ref, so ref means a person with a job. But «Our ref: 4471» is followed by a number, so here ref means reference, a code used to find a letter or document.
explain: Ref can also be a verb. «The teacher agreed to ref the match» means she will referee it. Always ask: does the sentence need a person, a number, or an action?
fact: Ref is short for referee: the official who makes sure players follow the rules.
fact: Ref can be a verb too: to ref a game means to referee it.
fact: Ref is also short for reference: a number or code used to find a letter, order or document, like «Ref: 4471».
fact: In letters and emails, «Our ref» shows the reference number to quote when you reply.
fact: Ref is an informal word, so in school writing use the full word, referee or reference, unless your teacher says otherwise.
exercise: «Relax, he's at the ref, not us.» What does ref mean here? | A kind of football boot | A code number used to find a letter | *A referee who runs the match | To read a book quickly
exercise: «Our ref: 4471, please quote it in your reply.» What is ref in this sentence? | A type of ball | A referee blowing a whistle | A player on the team | *A reference number to quote
exercise: Fans shout, «Come on, ref!» Who is the ref in a football match? | A player who scores the goals | A fan in the crowd | *The official who makes sure players follow the rules | The team's coach
test: Mo says, «The coach asked me to ref the game on Saturday.» What does ref mean here? | To score in the game | To buy tickets for the game | *To referee the game | To lose the game
test: Ella finds a letter that says, «Ref: 9083. Please quote this in all replies.» What does Ref show? | *The reference number for finding the letter | The date the letter was sent | A hidden message from a friend | The name of the referee who wrote it
exam: Which sentence uses ref as a reference number? | Referees run about 10 to 12 km a match | Jack blames the ref for the loss | *Please quote our ref: 4471 in all your letters | Fans shout, «Come on, ref!»
